{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 2, :comments ["And now they add — this generation continues to sin." "<b>They offer them</b> — כתבונם is like כתבונתם, as in: וצורם לבלות שאול וצורתם (their shape/guile)." "<b>They say of them</b> — people offer them for mockery, for they kiss the Baalim, which are the forms of calves, as in: וכל הפה אשר לא נשק לו (and every mouth that did not kiss him). And they shed innocent blood, and this is: ודמיו עליו יטוש (and his blood will be cast upon him). And they are the opposite of all men, for a man kisses a man who is his fellow and slaughters calves for his food."], :book :hosea, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 13, :notes {2 "Resolved זבחי אדם as 'slaughters calves,' following the contextual logic; the Hebrew is compressed and the syntax of עגלים/אדם is inverted between the two clauses."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Hosea -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/daat/olam_hatanah/mefaresh.asp?book=15&perek=1&mefaresh=ezra"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:51:08.193682583Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}